{"chunk_id":"R2-2405271-002","collection":"ran2_tdoc_chunks","metadata":{"source":["FUTUREWEI"],"tdocNumber":"R2-2405271","title":"Discussion on Data Collection for UE-side Model Training"},"point_id":"817783050785628184"}
Many discussions involved the debate of the location of the server for UE-side data collection, either inside or outside MNO’s networks. The concept often messed up with the ownership of the server, making the discussion more complex. Ownership of the server Let’s first clarify the ownership of the server. One question asked during the post-meeting email discussion, was whether a server located within the MNO's network is deemed to be MNO-owned, whereas one located outside is not under MNO ownership. Although more companies think that a server located within an MNO's network is typically considered to be MNO-owned, we believe the answer is not that straightforward. We think the key here is the definition of “ownership”. In the case the UE vendor renting server space from the MNO, the ownership of the server should be the UE vendor (while the MNO can be like a cloud server provider). In this case, the collected data should be also owned by the UE vendor. It is like one rent the apartment from the landlord, he/she has the ownership of his/her personal stuff inside the apartment. When we talk about ownership here, the collected data (the content) is more important than the physical device that stores it.

